# ALL.mask -- R-409 line masks for this container (entry<TAB>L<n>-or-python-regex<TAB>reason); the same rules on the oracle's stream and on SCRIP's, a masked line replaced by its marker and never deleted.
variable-size-get	PART:^type=\S+ \*x=\S+ bytes allocated=(-?[0-9]+)$	the byte count iconx reports for a value is its own allocator's block size, a machine value no program computes and SCRIP does not impersonate: MEASURED 2026-11-17 on SCRIP cdd18cb229, variable-size-get run on the oracle iconx and on SCRIP gives eight lines of type=T *x=N bytes allocated=B, every T and N equal and only B different (string 32 against the oracle's 8, the empty cset 0 against 48, the lists 160, 208 and 224 against 224, 128 and 144, the set 320 against 336), both ending in run-time error 108 at line 17 with status 1; masked in both streams, only the number, so the type, the size and the words stay graded (Lon 2026-11-17 13:4x CST: "remember the masking of machine/system specific is how a test passes.")
